IMPORT prelude

-- Vigilante Corps Act 1967 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a member of the Vigilante Corps: who must take the oath and
-- gets a certificate (ss 10, 11), resigning and being discharged (ss 12, 23), returning Government property (s 13), desertion
-- (s 14), the disciplinary punishments, compensation orders and appeals for Schedule offences (ss 16 to 18, 22, 24), threatening
-- or insulting a police officer or member (s 25), losing or damaging equipment (s 26), witnesses (s 27), deductions from pay
-- (ss 29, 30) and outside work by a full-time member (Schedule item 27).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/VCA1967.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; no later
-- amendment is annotated in the text. The deposit's meta file records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026. THE
-- ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS IN THE DEPOSIT IS OUT OF STEP WITH THE BODY BY ONE NUMBER (it lists "2. Short title"); this encoding
-- follows the body's numbering, in which s 1 is the short title and s 2 the interpretation section.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0133 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a member (volunteer or national serviceman) actually meets. Not encoded: raising,
-- functions, units and disbandment of the Corps (ss 3 to 9), the commencement and place of detention and persons unlawfully at
-- large (ss 19 to 21; s 21(2) is noted only), the regulation-making power (s 31), the transitional provision (s 32), and the
-- Schedule offences other than item 27 (they are treated as a single "Schedule offence" input).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Vigilante Corps Act 1967 -- service and discipline`

-- s 2: "officer" means any member "not below the rank of assistant unit leader"; "subordinate officer" means a member "below
-- the rank of assistant unit leader". s 4: the Corps consists of "(a) national servicemen; and (b) volunteers who have been
-- enrolled in the Corps by the Commandant". s 7(1): members "shall not be police officers within the meaning of the Police
-- Force Act 2004".
DECLARE Member HAS
    `is a national serviceman` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is below the rank of assistant unit leader` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a full-time member` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a subordinate officer` IF `the member`'s `is below the rank of assistant unit leader`

§§ `10, 11 -- oath and certificate`

-- s 10(1): every member "shall take an oath or affirmation"; (2) a member who refuses is liable to "a fine not exceeding $1,000
-- or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"; (3) "This section shall not apply to members of the Corps who
-- are national servicemen."
-- s 11(1): a certificate "shall be issued to every member"; (2) "No certificate shall be issued to any member of the Corps who
-- is a national serviceman."
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must take the oath` IF NOT `the member`'s `is a national serviceman`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member, `refused the oath` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing the oath is an offence` IF `must take the oath` `the member` AND `refused the oath`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is issued a certificate` IF NOT `the member`'s `is a national serviceman`

§§ `12, 23 -- resignation and discharge`

-- s 12(1): "Any member of the Corps, who is enrolled as a volunteer, may resign by giving to the Commandant 14 days' notice in
-- writing". (2) the Commandant may discharge a member "not likely to become or remain useful in the Corps".
-- s 23: a member "called up for national service in the Corps" shall not be discharged under s 12 "except with the prior
-- approval of the proper authority" under the national service law.
-- INFERENCE: s 12(1) gives the right to resign only to volunteers; the text gives a national serviceman no route to resign.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member, `notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `days of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may resign by notice` IF
        (NOT `the member`'s `is a national serviceman`)
    AND `notice is in writing`
    AND `days of notice` AT LEAST 14

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member, `Commandant thinks not likely to be useful` IS A BOOLEAN, `proper authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be discharged` IF
        `Commandant thinks not likely to be useful`
    AND (    (NOT `the member`'s `is a national serviceman`)
         OR  `proper authority approved`)

§§ `13, 26 -- Government property`

-- s 13(1): a member leaving the Corps "shall before leaving deliver up in good order (fair wear and tear only excepted)" arms,
-- uniform and other Government property; (2) neglect: "a fine not exceeding $500 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 3 months, and shall, in addition be liable to pay the value". s 26(1): pawning, selling, losing by neglect or damaging
-- equipment: the same $500 or 3 months, "in addition" the value; (3) "The Commandant may in minor cases compound such offences."
-- Note: ss 13(2) and 26(1) say fine OR imprisonment -- unlike ss 10, 24, 25 and 27 they do not add "or to both".
GIVEN `value of the property` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a court may order for unreturned or lost property` MEANS 500 PLUS `value of the property`

§§ `14 -- desertion`

-- s 14(1): a member who "unlawfully absents himself from duty under circumstances which show that he has the intention of not
-- returning to his duty" is deemed to have deserted: "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months" (no fine is provided).
-- (2) any police officer may arrest without warrant on reasonable grounds.
GIVEN `absent unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN, `circumstances show intention not to return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is deemed to have deserted` IF `absent unlawfully` AND `circumstances show intention not to return`

§§ `16, 17 -- disciplinary punishments`

-- s 16(1): a disciplinary officer finding a subordinate officer guilty of a Schedule offence may impose ANY ONE of: "(a) detention
-- for a period not exceeding 40 days; (b) a fine not exceeding $200; (c) stoppage of leave for any period not exceeding 28 days;
-- (d) restriction of privileges for any period not exceeding 14 days; (e) extra duty or drill for any period not exceeding
-- 7 days; (f) reprimand; (g) caution." (2) for reduction in rank he must refer to the Commandant, who "may reduce the rank ... or
-- impose any one of the punishments" in (1).
-- s 17(1): for an officer, a commanding officer "may reduce the rank of the officer or impose any one of the punishments which
-- a disciplinary officer may impose under section 16(1)".
DECLARE Punishment IS ONE OF
    `detention`
    `a fine`
    `stoppage of leave`
    `restriction of privileges`
    `extra duty or drill`
    `reprimand`
    `caution`
    `reduction in rank`

DECLARE Decider IS ONE OF
    `a disciplinary officer, for a subordinate officer`
    `the Commandant, on a referral`
    `a commanding officer, for an officer`

-- The quantity is days for detention, leave, privileges and extra duty, and dollars for a fine; it is ignored otherwise.
GIVEN `the punishment` IS A Punishment, `quantity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within section 16(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the punishment`
    WHEN `detention` THEN `quantity` AT MOST 40
    WHEN `a fine` THEN `quantity` AT MOST 200
    WHEN `stoppage of leave` THEN `quantity` AT MOST 28
    WHEN `restriction of privileges` THEN `quantity` AT MOST 14
    WHEN `extra duty or drill` THEN `quantity` AT MOST 7
    WHEN `reprimand` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `caution` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reduction in rank` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the decider` IS A Decider, `the punishment` IS A Punishment, `quantity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may impose` IF
    CONSIDER `the decider`
    WHEN `a disciplinary officer, for a subordinate officer` THEN `is within section 16(1)` `the punishment` `quantity`
    WHEN `the Commandant, on a referral` THEN `the punishment` EQUALS `reduction in rank` OR `is within section 16(1)` `the punishment` `quantity`
    WHEN `a commanding officer, for an officer` THEN `the punishment` EQUALS `reduction in rank` OR `is within section 16(1)` `the punishment` `quantity`

§§ `16(4), 17(3), 22, 24 -- compensation, fines and prosecution`

-- s 16(4): a disciplinary officer may order a subordinate officer to pay "compensation not exceeding $50"; s 17(3): a
-- commanding officer may order an officer to pay "compensation not exceeding $100".
-- s 24(1): instead of discipline, a member accused of a Schedule offence may "be prosecuted in any court" -- "a fine not
-- exceeding $500 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or to both"; (2) the court may order "compensation not
-- exceeding $1,000"; (4) "No prosecution under this section shall be instituted without the previous sanction in writing of a
-- commanding officer."
-- s 22 and s 24(3): compensation does not prejudice a civil remedy "for the recovery of damages beyond the amount of
-- compensation".
DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `disciplinary proceedings against a subordinate officer`
    `disciplinary proceedings against an officer`
    `prosecution in court`

GIVEN `the forum` IS A Forum
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a Schedule offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the forum`
    WHEN `disciplinary proceedings against a subordinate officer` THEN 200
    WHEN `disciplinary proceedings against an officer` THEN 200
    WHEN `prosecution in court` THEN 500

GIVEN `the forum` IS A Forum
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum compensation for a Schedule offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the forum`
    WHEN `disciplinary proceedings against a subordinate officer` THEN 50
    WHEN `disciplinary proceedings against an officer` THEN 100
    WHEN `prosecution in court` THEN 1000

GIVEN `sanction in writing by a commanding officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution for a Schedule offence may be instituted` IF `sanction in writing by a commanding officer`

GIVEN `damages proved` IS A NUMBER, `compensation paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the civil claim left after compensation` MEANS
    IF `damages proved` GREATER THAN `compensation paid` THEN `damages proved` MINUS `compensation paid` ELSE 0

§§ `16(3), 17(2), 18 -- appeals`

-- s 16(3): a subordinate officer may appeal "to a commanding officer within 14 days from the date of the decision"; s 17(2): an
-- officer may appeal "to the Commissioner within 14 days". In both, "any punishment imposed shall be suspended pending the
-- determination of the appeal".
-- s 18: on appeal the punishment substituted "shall not in any event be greater or more severe than that originally imposed".
-- Severity is compared here only within one kind of punishment (days or dollars); the text gives no scale across kinds.
DECLARE Appellate IS ONE OF
    `a commanding officer`
    `the Commissioner`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A Appellate
`the appeal lies to` MEANS
    IF `is a subordinate officer` `the member` THEN `a commanding officer` ELSE `the Commissioner`

GIVEN `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF `days since the decision` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `an appeal has been lodged` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appeal is determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the punishment is suspended` IF `an appeal has been lodged` AND (NOT `the appeal is determined`)

GIVEN `original quantity` IS A NUMBER, `substituted quantity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substituted punishment is permitted` IF `substituted quantity` AT MOST `original quantity`

§§ `25 -- threatening or insulting`

-- s 25(1): a member "who threatens or insults any police officer or member of senior or equal rank when that police officer or
-- member is on duty, or when such threat or insult relates to or is consequent on the discharge of duty" commits an offence:
-- "a fine not exceeding $1,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both". (2) arrest without warrant.
-- INFERENCE: "of senior or equal rank" is read as qualifying "member" only, so any police officer is protected. The text can
-- also be read as qualifying both; a Corps rank and a police rank have no stated comparison.
GIVEN `the target is a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the target is a member of senior or equal rank` IS A BOOLEAN, `the target was on duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `it relates to the target's duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the threat or insult is an offence under section 25` IF
        (`the target is a police officer` OR `the target is a member of senior or equal rank`)
    AND (`the target was on duty` OR `it relates to the target's duty`)

§§ `27 -- witnesses`

-- s 27(3): a person required to attend disciplinary proceedings "who without reasonable excuse fails to do so" -- "a fine not
-- exceeding $100 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding one month or to both". (2) privilege as in a court is preserved.
GIVEN `required by notice to attend` IS A BOOLEAN, `attended` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to attend as a witness is an offence` IF
    `required by notice to attend` AND (NOT `attended`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `29, 30 -- deductions from pay`

-- s 29(2): deductions for compensation, fines and sums awarded "shall not exceed such sums as will leave to him less than $1 a
-- day", and no deduction "greater than is sufficient to make good" the loss or to pay the sum awarded.
-- s 30(2)(a): no person is treated as absent, imprisoned or detained "unless the absence, imprisonment or detention has lasted
-- 6 hours or more, or the absence prevented the absentee from fulfilling any duty"; (d) "no period of less than 24 hours shall be
-- reckoned as more than one day".
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `ordinary pay due` IS A NUMBER, `days of pay` IS A NUMBER, `sum awarded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be deducted` MEANS
    IF `ordinary pay due` MINUS `days of pay` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `the lesser of` `sum awarded` (`ordinary pay due` MINUS `days of pay`)

GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER, `the absence prevented a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be treated as absent` IF `hours` AT LEAST 6 OR `the absence prevented a duty`

GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be reckoned as more than one day` IF `hours` AT LEAST 24

§§ `Schedule item 27 -- outside work`

-- Schedule item 27: "Being a full-time member, engages in any trade or employment without the permission of the Commissioner."
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member, `engages in a trade or employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `Commissioner permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `outside work is a Schedule offence` IF
    `the member`'s `is a full-time member` AND `engages in a trade or employment` AND (NOT `Commissioner permitted it`)
